  "notes": "Port list is the datasheet's DEFAULT service mode, eth-2x50ge-2x25ge-2x10gf-14xgf-mode, not its maxima: the same cages can be re-partitioned with \"set service-mode card-bandwidth-mode\" into eth-2x50ge-6x10gf-14xgf, eth-2x25ge-12x10gf-14xgf or eth-16x10gf-14xgf, which is how the sheet quotes \"up to 16x10GE\" and \"26 GE optical\". The four electrical GE ports are present in every mode and are modelled as RJ45. MACsec is limited to specific cages - 50GE on ports 26/27, 25GE/10GE/GE on 24/25, 10GE/GE on 22/23 - so a MACsec requirement pins the service mode as well. No PoE in any configuration: this is a carrier router with AC or -48 V DC feeds (-40 to 65 C, 125.1 W typical), not a PoE PSE. FE(o)/FE(e) are supported on the GE cages by software, so a 100M link here is a configured 1G port, not a separate interface.",
